# Ops design language (locked v1.2)

Source of truth: `docs/ops-design/DND_OPS_DESIGN_LANGUAGE_GUIDE_V1_2_LOCKED.md`

This rule does **not** authorize feature work, IA changes, desktop-shell work, or production page migration. If the locked guide conflicts with a requested implementation, **STOP and report the conflict**. Do not invent tokens, exceptions, or primitives to proceed.

## Scope

Applies to the new Ops design island: `client/src/ops/**`, plus explicitly migrated production files listed in the globs (currently Gift Vouchers collection, Gift Voucher detail, Promo Codes, Manual Review, Sync, Communications, Payments, Users, Cabins list, Cabin detail, Reservations collection, Reservation detail, Home Dashboard, Messaging, Cleaning Settings panels, Reviews, and Calendar index/month). Work Windows and Cleaning Calendar remain legacy.

`client/src/pages/ops/**` is otherwise legacy until an explicit migration slice. Do not drive-by rewrite it. Do not fail CI against that tree from this rule except for files listed in `MIGRATED_OPS_FILES` (`client/scripts/check-ops-design.cjs`).

## MUST

- New Ops UI uses canonical primitives in `client/src/ops/primitives/`.
- New Ops UI uses semantic `--ops-*` tokens only.
- Light and dark use the same token names. No `dark:` / `html.dark` / raw `gray-*` styling.
- No public-site editorial styling. No Playfair. No `font-serif` / `font-heading` / `font-script` as Ops styling (ops.css may neutralize those classes to Inter).
- No raw visual hex outside `client/src/ops/ops.css` (and the P0A test mirror `client/src/ops/tokens/opsTokenNames.js`).
- No arbitrary one-off Tailwind visual values (`p-[13px]`, `rounded-[7px]`, `text-[#…]`, `z-[9999]`) when a locked token exists.
- No `window.confirm`, `alert`, or `prompt`. Use `OpsConfirmDialog` / canonical overlays.
- No new status color or label maps outside `client/src/ops/status/opsStatusRegistry.js`.
- No new overlay system. Modal / Sheet / Confirm come from `client/src/ops/primitives/` and `opsOverlay.js`.
- No new component library (Radix, Headless UI, shadcn, Framer Motion, focus-trap packages) without explicit approval.
- Production migrations must preserve business behavior. Visual change only when the slice says so.
- Mobile and desktop share semantics, not necessarily layout.
- Register every approved deviation in `docs/ops-design/OPS_DESIGN_EXCEPTION_REGISTER.md`.

## MUST NOT

- Do not migrate Work Windows, Cleaning Calendar, Insights, Conversion, or other production pages unless the current slice names them.
- Do not add `/ops/design-system` to operator navigation.
- Do not treat this rule as permission to start the desktop sidebar, command search, or P0+ shell work.

## Checks

Run from `client/`:

```bash
npm run test:ops-design
```
